    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Summary\nHandlers and services return raw `fmt.Errorf(...)` for conditions that are **transient or expected**, and `backend/internal/httpd/envelope.go` maps any non-`apierr` error to `INTERNAL_ERROR` / `500`. As a result, transient DB contention (#3963), client-state conditions, and genuine faults all surface as **identical opaque 500s** \u2014 the reliability signal is polluted by non-faults, and the real cause is only visible in the daemon log, never in the API response.\n\n## Where\n- `backend/internal/httpd/envelope.go` \u2014 the `INTERNAL_ERROR` fallback for untyped errors.\n- Example offender: `backend/internal/service/session/workspace_files.go` \u2192 `sessionWorkspaceRecord` wraps `GetSession` as `fmt.Errorf(\"get %s: %w\", \u2026)` (untyped \u2192 500).\n\n## Reproduction\n1. `rg \"envelope.WriteError\" backend/internal/httpd/controllers` and follow each to the service call it forwards \u2014 the ones returning plain `fmt.Errorf` (not `apierr.*`) become opaque 500s.\n2. Drive any such handler while the DB is under contention (#3963): the response is a `500` with code `INTERNAL_ERROR` and no specific `error_code`, indistinguishable from a real server fault.\n\n## Suggested fix\n- Map transient/contention DB errors to a typed `503` (retryable) with a stable code, and expected states to typed `4xx`, so the 5xx surface reflects only real server faults.\n- Land Sentry error capture (PRs #4180 desktop / #4181 mobile) so the remaining genuine 500s carry a grouped stack and root cause.\n\n## Related\n- #3963, #3649, #2699, #3408 (instances of the opacity); #4180 / #4181 (visibility)\n",
